{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column definitions can contain strings, VNodes, Vue components, or renderer functions for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"header"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cell"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"footer"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aggregatedCell"},{"type":"text","value":". Use the adapter's rendering utilities so each form is mounted correctly and receives its table context."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"flexrender-vs-flexrender","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FlexRender"},{"type":"text","value":" vs "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"flexRender"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FlexRender"},{"type":"text","value":" is the recommended Vue component. Its shorthand props accept exactly one "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cell"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"header"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"footer"},{"type":"text","value":" object:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport { FlexRender } from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <th v-for=\"header in headerGroup.headers\" :key=\"header.id\">\n    <FlexRender v-if=\"!header.isPlaceholder\" :header=\"header\" />\n  </th>\n\n  <td v-for=\"cell in row.getVisibleCells()\" :key=\"cell.id\">\n    <FlexRender :cell=\"cell\" />\n  </td>\n</template>","lang":"vue"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For cells, the component selects "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aggregatedCell"},{"type":"text","value":" for aggregated rows, falls back to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cell"},{"type":"text","value":", and renders nothing for grouping placeholders. Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":":footer=\"header\""},{"type":"text","value":" for a header object from a footer group."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tables created by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createTableHook"},{"type":"text","value":" also expose an app-aware component as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.FlexRender"},{"type":"text","value":". Because it is stored as a value, render it with Vue's dynamic component syntax:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<component :is=\"table.FlexRender\" :cell=\"cell\" />","lang":"vue"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"flexRender"},{"type":"text","value":" is the lower-level function for a renderable value and its props:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { flexRender } from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n\nflexRender(cell.column.columnDef.cell, cell.getContext())","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"It passes primitive values through, preserves returned VNodes, and creates VNodes for Vue component objects. It does not choose grouped-cell renderers or suppress grouping placeholders."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The component still supports the older low-level "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"render"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"props"},{"type":"text","value":" pair:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<FlexRender :render=\"cell.column.columnDef.cell\" :props=\"cell.getContext()\" />","lang":"vue"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Prefer the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cell"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"header"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"footer"},{"type":"text","value":" shorthand for new code. Placeholder headers remain the caller's layout decision, so check "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"header.isPlaceholder"},{"type":"text","value":" unless a spanning-header layout intentionally renders one."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"flexrender-vs-flexrender","text":"FlexRender vs flexRender","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nColumn definitions can contain strings, VNodes, Vue components, or renderer functions for `header`, `cell`, `footer`, and `aggregatedCell`. Use the adapter's rendering utilities so each form is mounted correctly and receives its table context.\n\n## `FlexRender` vs `flexRender`\n\n`FlexRender` is the recommended Vue component. Its shorthand props accept exactly one `cell`, `header`, or `footer` object:\n\n```vue\n<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport { FlexRender } from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <th v-for=\"header in headerGroup.headers\" :key=\"header.id\">\n    <FlexRender v-if=\"!header.isPlaceholder\" :header=\"header\" />\n  </th>\n\n  <td v-for=\"cell in row.getVisibleCells()\" :key=\"cell.id\">\n    <FlexRender :cell=\"cell\" />\n  </td>\n</template>\n```\n\nFor cells, the component selects `aggregatedCell` for aggregated rows, falls back to `cell`, and renders nothing for grouping placeholders. Use `:footer=\"header\"` for a header object from a footer group.\n\nTables created by `createTableHook` also expose an app-aware component as `table.FlexRender`. Because it is stored as a value, render it with Vue's dynamic component syntax:\n\n```vue\n<component :is=\"table.FlexRender\" :cell=\"cell\" />\n```\n\n`flexRender` is the lower-level function for a renderable value and its props:\n\n```ts\nimport { flexRender } from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n\nflexRender(cell.column.columnDef.cell, cell.getContext())\n```\n\nIt passes primitive values through, preserves returned VNodes, and creates VNodes for Vue component objects. It does not choose grouped-cell renderers or suppress grouping placeholders.\n\nThe component still supports the older low-level `render`/`props` pair:\n\n```vue\n<FlexRender :render=\"cell.column.columnDef.cell\" :props=\"cell.getContext()\" />\n```\n\nPrefer the `cell`, `header`, and `footer` shorthand for new code. Placeholder headers remain the caller's layout decision, so check `header.isPlaceholder` unless a spanning-header layout intentionally renders one.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: FlexRender (Vue) Guide\n---\n\nColumn definitions can contain strings, VNodes, Vue components, or renderer functions for `header`, `cell`, `footer`, and `aggregatedCell`. Use the adapter's rendering utilities so each form is mounted correctly and receives its table context.\n\n## `FlexRender` vs `flexRender`\n\n`FlexRender` is the recommended Vue component. Its shorthand props accept exactly one `cell`, `header`, or `footer` object:\n\n```vue\n<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport { FlexRender } from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <th v-for=\"header in headerGroup.headers\" :key=\"header.id\">\n    <FlexRender v-if=\"!header.isPlaceholder\" :header=\"header\" />\n  </th>\n\n  <td v-for=\"cell in row.getVisibleCells()\" :key=\"cell.id\">\n    <FlexRender :cell=\"cell\" />\n  </td>\n</template>\n```\n\nFor cells, the component selects `aggregatedCell` for aggregated rows, falls back to `cell`, and renders nothing for grouping placeholders. Use `:footer=\"header\"` for a header object from a footer group.\n\nTables created by `createTableHook` also expose an app-aware component as `table.FlexRender`. Because it is stored as a value, render it with Vue's dynamic component syntax:\n\n```vue\n<component :is=\"table.FlexRender\" :cell=\"cell\" />\n```\n\n`flexRender` is the lower-level function for a renderable value and its props:\n\n```ts\nimport { flexRender } from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n\nflexRender(cell.column.columnDef.cell, cell.getContext())\n```\n\nIt passes primitive values through, preserves returned VNodes, and creates VNodes for Vue component objects. It does not choose grouped-cell renderers or suppress grouping placeholders.\n\nThe component still supports the older low-level `render`/`props` pair:\n\n```vue\n<FlexRender :render=\"cell.column.columnDef.cell\" :props=\"cell.getContext()\" />\n```\n\nPrefer the `cell`, `header`, and `footer` shorthand for new code. Placeholder headers remain the caller's layout decision, so check `header.isPlaceholder` unless a spanning-header layout intentionally renders one.\n"}
